<title>RUSSIA: Russian MOST-Bank changes president.</title>
<headline>Russian MOST-Bank changes president.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most-Bank, one of Russia's biggest banks, has appointed its chairman Boris Khait as president, the bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Khait replaces Vladimir Gusinsky, who became president of ZAO Media-MOST, part of the Most group, which holds shares in media companies, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The Central Bank had not yet approved Khait's appointment, it said.</p>
<p>--Maxim Filimonov, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
